{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "workspace-one-uem",
  "description": "One page of the version-2 PascalCase device search envelope. Covers: the {\"Value\": n} scalar wrapper on Id and LocationGroupId; the future-timestamp clamp (a tenant east of UTC emits zone-less local times that read as ahead of now, and runZero rejects the WHOLE record for a future first/last-seen, so _clamp_ts holds it at now); the 0001-01-01 never-sentinel; the zone-less timestamp that parse_time would otherwise abort on; friendly names with spaces and apostrophes being kept as attributes rather than promoted to hostnames; and loopback/link-local suppression with the MacAddress-only fallback interface. check_determinism is off and `ids` is unasserted for a harness reason: the id is scoped by the tenant host (base_url.split(\"://\")[-1]), which under the fixture server is 127.0.0.1:<ephemeral port> and so differs between runs. Also note the aw-tenant-code header cannot be asserted: the harness only records Authorization and Cookie.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "username": "fixture-admin",
    "password": "fixture-password",
    "api_key": "fixture-tenant-code",
    "page_size": "500"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "name": "device-search",
      "match": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/mdm/devices/search"},
